Client change:

```js
let last = '';

async function poll() {
  const text = await (await fetch('/api/metrics')).text();
  if (text === last) return; // nothing rewritten since the last poll
  last = text;
  const { rows, computed_at } = JSON.parse(text);
  render(rows);
  document.getElementById('stamp').textContent = new Date(computed_at).toLocaleTimeString();
}

poll();
setInterval(poll, 15000);
```

Compare the whole body, not just `computed_at`. If a poll lands mid-rewrite and sees a partial rollup, a `computed_at` check could skip the complete version that shares its timestamp. Comparing the body means the next poll corrects it.

